    {
      "_id": "qElkeL36RuPuZin6",
      "_key": "!actors.items!i13I7aDguqmtP1xY.qElkeL36RuPuZin6",
      "name": "Headwinds",
      "img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-weapons-orange.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "sort": 700,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "flags": {},
      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Choose one of the following options. Once the draconimbus uses an option, it must recharge that headwind before it can use it again (see Multiple Heads). The draconimbus can't use a headwind if the corresponding head is dissipated.</p><ol><li><strong>Electric Wind.</strong> <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 20 Dexterity, each creature in a 100-foot-long, 5-foot-wide Line. A creature wearing metal armour has Disadvantage on the saving throw. <em>Failure:</em> 35 (10d6) Lightning damage. <em>Failure by 5 or More:</em> The target is Paralysed until the start of its next turn and drops any held creatures or objects. <em>Success:</em> Half damage.</li><li><strong>Freezing Wind.</strong> <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 20 Constitution, each creature in a 60-foot Cone. <em>Failure:</em> 21 (6d6) Cold damage, and the target's Speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</li><li><strong>Maddening Wind.</strong> <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 20 Wisdom, each creature in a 60-foot Cone. <em>Failure:</em> 26 (4d12) Psychic damage, and the target immediately moves up to its Speed directly towards the nearest body of water it can see. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</li><li><strong>Thunderous Wind.</strong> <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 20 Constitution, each creature in a 40-foot Emanation originating from the draconimbus. <em>Failure:</em> 33 (6d10) Thunder damage, and the target is Deafened and knocked Prone. <em>Success:</em> Half damage only.</li></ol>",
          "chat": ""
